## Final Verdict

**PASS — `all_three_array_positions_stamped`.** Runtime-pushed Niagara User Array
values ARE GPU-visible in a Grid2D simulation stage on UE 5.6.1.

| Measure | Value |
|---|---|
| CPU getter count | 3 (`[128,128,0] [256,256,0] [384,128,0]` via `set_niagara_array_position`) |
| RT full scan (step 16) nonzero | 71 |
| Channel sums R/G/B | 2836 / 2491 / 2735 — all three per-index channel stamps present |
| World | game_world (SIE), spawn/readback split commands |

## Root Cause (why S3 previously failed)

The engine was never the problem. The failing wiring was the hidden `User.*`
input-node route created by `insert_niagara_scratch_pad_custom_hlsl_for_pin
user_parameter_inputs`: GPU translation binds that DI input to a private
instance, while the Blueprint array setter writes the component override —
two different objects (CPU getter 3 / GPU 0 signature).

The engine-standard chain (externally documented in the ZukoMedia UE 5.1
Grid2D tutorial): `Blueprint -> User parameter -> Module input -> HLSL input`.
The Module-input step is what registers the binding in the compiled parameter
store. Corner-marker probes proved the HLSL executed while the array read
empty, isolating the binding as the sole failure point.

## The Working Recipe (3-step chain, fully automated)

```text
1. insert_niagara_scratch_pad_custom_hlsl_for_pin
     usage=Function, user_parameter_inputs=[Positions -> User.V1_Positions]
     (creates the HLSL node + Positions input pin)
2. rewire_niagara_custom_hlsl_input_to_module_parameter          [NEW C++ command]
     input Positions -> Module.Positions ParameterMapGet pin
     (registers scratch metadata, deletes orphaned hidden input node)
3. set_niagara_module_input_linked_parameter
     Positions -> User.V1_Positions
     (stack-level link; requires the scratch-metadata fallback patch)
```

Plus the usual G1 harness: DirectSet/TwoD stage, RT DI trio bind, SIE start,
split spawn/readback with real-time waits, full-RT scan judgment.

